+---
+id: dl-002-timestamps-come-from-an-injected-clock-not-the-domain-reading-the-wall-clock
+type: decision-log
+title: "Timestamps come from an injected Clock, not the domain reading the wall clock"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks need `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, as ISO-8601 date-time strings, to show how old a task is and
+what changed recently. Unlike the sequential id (`dl-001`), these have to reflect real elapsed time, so
+a closure counter cannot stand in for them. The obvious ways to get the current time — `Date.now()` or
+`new Date()` — are exactly what `r3-no-clock-or-randomness` forbids under `src/domain/`, where `list.ts`
+and `task.ts` live.
+
+## Decision
+
+`src/domain/list.ts` declares a `Clock` type, `() => string`, and `createTaskList(clock: Clock)` takes
+one as a required parameter. Every mutating method (`add`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`,
+`untag`) calls `clock()` once and passes the resulting string into the corresponding pure function in
+`task.ts` (`createTask`, `completeTask`, `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag`, `removeTag`), which stamps
+it onto the returned task. The one call to `new Date().toISOString()` in the whole codebase lives in
+`src/index.ts`, outside `src/domain/`, as the default `clock` passed to `createTaskList` by
+`createTodoList`.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `src/domain/` still never reads the wall clock — compliant with `r3-no-clock-or-randomness` — and
+  every domain function stays pure and deterministic given its arguments.
+- `createTodoList` keeps working with no arguments for existing callers (it defaults to the real clock),
+  while tests and other callers can inject a fake `Clock` for deterministic timestamps.
+- Every call to `tag`, `untag`, `rename`, `complete` or `reopen` bumps `updatedAt`, even when the
+  requested change is a no-op (e.g. tagging a task with a tag it already has, or renaming it to its
+  current title): the action, not the resulting diff, is what counts as "a change". If the app later
+  needs "no-op calls don't bump `updatedAt`", that will need each `change`-like helper in `list.ts` to
+  compare before and after.
