@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+---
+id: task-002-record-createdat-and-updatedat-on-every-task
+type: task
+title: "Record createdAt and updatedAt on every task"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Track how old a task is and what changed recently: every task gets `createdAt` and `updatedAt`, as
+ISO-8601 date-time strings. On `add` the two are the same. Every change to a task — completing,
+reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging it — sets `updatedAt` to the time of that change.
+
+## What I did
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts`: added `createdAt: string` and `updatedAt: string` to `Task`. `createTask(id,
+  input, createdAt)` now also takes the creation time and sets both fields to it. `completeTask`,
+  `reopenTask`, `renameTask`, `addTag` and `removeTag` each take an `updatedAt` parameter and stamp the
+  returned task with it, keeping every other field (including `createdAt`) as it was — same pattern as
+  `id` in `createTask`: the value comes in as a parameter, so the function stays pure.
+- `src/domain/list.ts`: added a `Clock` type (`() => string`, an ISO-8601 date-time string) and
+  `createTaskList` now takes a `clock` as a required parameter. It calls `clock()` once per mutating
+  call (`add`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag`) and threads the result into the `task.ts`
+  functions. No `Date.now()` or `new Date()` appears under `src/domain/`, per `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`:
+  the domain only ever sees a time that was handed to it.
+- `src/index.ts`: added `systemClock`, the one place that reads the real wall clock
+  (`new Date().toISOString()`), outside `src/domain/`. `createTodoList(clock = systemClock)` defaults to
+  it so existing callers are unaffected, but accepts an injected `Clock` for deterministic tests. Exported
+  the `Clock` type.
+- `test/list.test.ts`: added a `fakeClock` helper (returns a fixed sequence of timestamps, repeating the
+  last one) and two tests: one that a new task's `createdAt` and `updatedAt` both equal the time it was
+  added, and one that `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag` and `untag` each advance `updatedAt` while
+  `createdAt` stays put. Updated the existing "adds an open task" test to allow for the two new fields.
+
+All 10 tests pass (`npm test`).
